<title>UK: Clarke says business investment to grow 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Clarke says business investment to grow 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Chancellor of the Exchequer Kenneth Clarke said on Tuesday he expects business investment in Britain to continue to grow strongly.</p>
<p>&quot;I expect business investment to continue to grow strongly: by almost 10 percent next year,&quot; Clarke said.</p>
<p>He said investment had grown by six percent so far this year.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717.</p>
